From ce57da39701285c2fcdb6af36feffe8bfb0b10b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:37:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Start games sooner and bring the menu back faster

The launcher starts before the menu lets go of the screen and sound, so
its Python and the game's configuration overlap the menu's teardown;
Canica's launcher holds the emulator back while /var/run/canica/menu-busy
exists. When it writes /var/run/canica/game-ended (the emulator is gone,
gameStop scripts are next), the window and sound come back on this thread
while another reads the launcher to its end. game-end scripts run beside
the way back, and the return fade is half as long.

Every other configgen launch also goes through the save adapter, with
--es-no-resume, when the installed adapter knows that option. The menu
starts the adapter's warm launcher after its start event, so even the
first game skips loading configgen.

Font textures keep a copy of their glyphs, so coming back re-uploads each
texture once instead of rendering every glyph again (29 fonts: 0.5-0.7 s
to under 0.01 s on the RG35XX H).

Each step is written to /var/run/canica-launch-timing.log while that file
exists, to measure launches on the handheld.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
